notes.body:
@rbalint Can you at least elaborate which issues were raised, other than licensing (which has already been addressed/reverted)? I don't see any other issues in that mailing list thread.

All I see on that thread is @rknall showing support for the plugin API changes (except license check).

I didn't know a cost/benefit analysis was expected, I have never seen anyone do that in this project, but I can help with that too.

This change and the ones that it reverts are frustrating because there are some arguably good changes that are coupled with some arguably bad ones. I think the plugin metainformation is a good idea, as well as a UI for adding plugins. However, I really don't like the extra plugin ABI variables. They _must_ be updated when switching release versions, and at the same time are easy to overlook. They map 1:1 to major release versions, so why not just use the major release versions? I also don't like appending the ABI version to the plugin filename on macOS and Windows, e.g. plugin.dll.1. 

I'm going to merge this. Hopefully we can bring the good changes back in in separate changes as suggested in an earlier comment.

@jvalverde this project clearly isn't meeting your expectations, and neither am I. I'm not sure what to tell you in that regard.

